.TH LIUXIN-INGEST-WEB 1 "2026-10-23" "LiuXin-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liuxin-ingest-web \- register remote files or acquire verified managed copies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liuxin ingest web
.I URL
.RB [ \-\-register-only | \-\-download ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest web
.I URL
.B \-\-list
.RI [ connection/output-options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest web
.BR \-\-status " " RUN_UUID
.RI [ connection/output-options ]
.br
.B liuxin ingest web
.BR \-\-resume " " RUN_UUID
.RI [ connection/job/output-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Walk a bounded HTTP(S) source using native or wget discovery.
Registration is the default and records matching remote links without acquiring
book payloads into storage. Navigation pages and robots rules are still fetched;
wget can also issue HEAD probes. A direct URL with an accepted file suffix can
be registered without contacting it.
.PP
An observation is not proof of current availability or ebook validity.
Download mode stages complete files, hashes them and publishes verified copies
through the existing storage manager. Identical bytes deduplicate; changed
bytes at a previously captured URL retain a new Asset and preserve the old one.
Neither mode automatically creates bibliographic Works, Expressions or
Manifestations, or a browsable mirror of the website.
.PP
Use a trailing slash for a directory root. Candidates must remain within the
selected scheme, authority and path subtree. Native requests and all payload
downloads check redirects before following them; the source host's robots
document is the path exception. Wget retains its own navigation/redirect
behavior and its results are filtered by the shared scope policy.
.SH ACTIONS
The following actions are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.B \-\-register-only
Record candidates without acquiring book contents. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-download
Acquire selected files into a configured writable managed Store.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List recorded candidates, historical captures and saved run IDs for URL without
contacting the site. Also finds runs whose workers never returned a report.
Do not supply crawl/download controls with inspection.
.TP
.BI \-\-status " RUN_UUID"
Inspect saved options, lease, received bytes, discovery state, last report and
per-file receipts. Omit URL and crawl/download controls.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " RUN_UUID"
Replay a saved run's exact controls and pinned destination UUID. Omit URL and
crawl/download controls. Connection, output and managed-job controls remain
available. See RESULTS AND RECOVERY below.
.SH SELECTION AND DESTINATION
.TP
.B \-\-registered-only
Select stored candidates for the same root URL without re-crawling navigation
pages. Combine with
.B \-\-download
to acquire recorded files later. Robots and selected payload requests still
occur during downloads.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Discover candidates without adding web-ingest tables, observations, run records
or staged files. Navigation requests still occur unless
.B \-\-registered-only
is also selected.
.TP
.BI \-\-extension " SUFFIX"
Accept this filename suffix; repeat for alternatives. Explicit suffixes replace
the default set of known book extensions, which excludes HTML navigation.
Use
.B \-\-extension html
to deliberately select HTML itself. Query-only download endpoints are not
detected by filename suffix.
.TP
.BI \-\-include " GLOB"
Narrow selection to matching URL globs. Repeat for alternatives and quote each
glob against shell expansion. A candidate must pass both the extension and glob
filters.
.TP
.BI \-\-crawler " native|wget"
Discovery adapter; default native. Wget must be installed to select wget.
LiuXin's HTTP driver still performs requested payload downloads.
.TP
.BI \-\-destination " STORE_UUID"
Writable managed Store to receive copies. Defaults to the configured default
Store. Only valid in download mode. The Store must report available capacity.
.TP
.BI \-\-state-directory " PATH"
Staging parent on the Core host. SQLite/APSW jobs default to
.B web-ingest/
beside the catalogue. Other database backends require an explicit directory
for downloads. Each run uses its own private directory and owned marker;
unsafe or unmarked pre-existing run directories are refused.
.SH LIMITS
MiB means 1,048,576 bytes. Integer limits must be positive except that depth and
free-space headroom permit zero. Timeouts must be positive; request pacing
permits zero to disable spacing.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-depth " N"
Navigation depth; default 5. Native discovery permits root-page links at depth
zero; the wget adapter renders a minimum recursive level of one.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-pages " N"
Native crawler page ceiling; default 1000. This option does not bound wget pages.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-files " N"
Selected candidates per run; default 1000. Reaching the ceiling still permits
acquisition of the selected subset within other budgets, but reports limited.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-file-mib " N"
Maximum retained bytes per file; default 256 MiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-total-mib " N"
Received file-payload budget across this run and its resumes; default 2048 MiB.
Failed transfers consume the budget. Navigation traffic, protocol overhead and
operating-system buffering are outside this counter. Unknown-length streams can
require one extra byte to detect overflow; it is counted but never published.
.TP
.BI \-\-min-free-mib " N"
Headroom on staging and destination volumes; default 1024 MiB. Capacity checks
allow for staging and a possible second publication copy. They do not reserve
capacity against other writers.
.TP
.BI \-\-requests-per-hour " RATE"
Request pacing. Defaults to the shared crawler preference, falling back to 1200
requests per hour. Zero disables spacing.
.TP
.BI \-\-request-timeout " SECONDS"
Network request timeout; default 30 seconds. Separate from the CLI wait timeout
and the Core job execution timeout.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-seconds " SECONDS"
Cooperative elapsed-time budget per attempt; default 3600 seconds.
A blocking read, hash check or publication can finish after the deadline.
.PP
Native HTML bodies are capped at 2,000,000 bytes per page. Both adapters cap
observed URLs at 100,000; wget retained output is capped at 8 MiB of decoded
characters. Wget has no equivalent per-page HTML ceiling or hard navigation
scratch quota. Prefer native discovery when this bound is needed.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
Use one explicit selector, or the configured connection defaults.
.TP
.BI \-\-system-root " DIRECTORY"
Read the system manifest in DIRECTORY.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " PROFILE"
Use a named profile, manifest path or directory containing a system manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-database " PATH"
Open Core against this local catalogue.
.TP
.BI \-\-db-type " TYPE"
Database backend for a direct database selector; default SQLite.
.TP
.BI \-\-core-endpoint " URL"
Connect to a running Core. Source requests, staging and Store access occur on
that host, not on the CLI host. Web execution requires trusted authority.
.TP
.BI \-\-core-token-file " PATH"
Read the remote Core bearer token from a private file.
.TP
.BI \-\-core-timeout " SECONDS"
Timeout for calls to remote Core; default 10 seconds. This is not a crawl timeout.
.TP
.BI \-\-job-ledger " PATH"
Select the local durable job database when opening a local Core.
SQLite catalogues default to a sidecar ledger.
.SH JOB AND OUTPUT OPTIONS
Registration and downloads submit managed jobs and wait by default.
.TP
.B \-\-detach
Return the submission receipt immediately. Acceptance does not prove acquisition
completed; inspect the job and web run later.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait-timeout " SECONDS"
Maximum CLI wait. Timing out does not cancel the Core job. By default there is
no explicit CLI wait deadline.
.TP
.BI \-\-poll-interval " SECONDS"
Job status poll interval; default 0.25 seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-job-timeout " SECONDS"
Core-side job execution timeout, separate from request and CLI wait timeouts.
.TP
.BI \-\-job-backend " NAME"
Request a configured job backend.
.TP
.B \-\-job-no-output
Ask the job manager not to retain worker output.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " TEXT"
Operator-visible job label.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Write JSON on the CLI host instead of standard output. Existing files are
refused unless replacement is explicit.
.TP
.B \-\-replace-output
Permit atomic replacement of an existing output file.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Emit compact JSON instead of indented JSON.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command help and exit.
.SH RESULTS AND RECOVERY
A completed job's
.B execution.result.run_id
is the web run UUID, distinct from its managed job ID. Use
.B liuxin jobs
for worker state and
.B liuxin ingest web \-\-status RUN_UUID
for saved selection and capture state. If a worker died before returning a
report, recover the run UUID with
.BR "liuxin ingest web URL \-\-list" .
.PP
Capture receipts retain source/final URLs, referring page when supplied,
retrieval time, HTTP validators, size, SHA-256 and Asset/Replica IDs.
Observation and retrieval times are Unix epoch milliseconds.
.B last_capture
is historical evidence, not a current availability check.
.B downloaded_bytes
counts received payload across attempts, including failed transfers.
.PP
Resume skips completed captures. Complete staged files are rehashed and reuse
the storage publication identity; partial transfers restart from byte zero.
An incomplete crawl is repeated while retaining previously selected candidates.
Completed discovery requires no further navigation request on resume.
.PP
An active lease prevents overlapping resumes. After a crash, wait for the lease
to expire. Missing or corrupt complete staging fails visibly; use a fresh run
if the staging cannot be recovered. An exhausted total byte budget stays
exhausted on resume. Start a new run to deliberately change its controls.
.PP
Successful publication removes the staged copy. Partial failure preserves
observations and prior successful acquisitions. Complete means the selected
bounded workflow finished, not that the entire website was inventoried.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful inspection, completed workflow, or accepted detached job.
.TP
.B 1
Job failure, CLI wait timeout, or a report marked partial, limited, failed or
interrupted.
.TP
.B 2
Argument errors or other dispatch/runtime errors handled by the CLI.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize a writable system directory and record a site:
.PP
.nf
liuxin init "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-register-only \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
.fi
.PP
Acquire only recorded EPUB links matching a quoted URL glob:
.PP
.nf
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-download \-\-registered-only \-\-extension epub \e
  \-\-include '*/selected-series/*' \-\-max-total-mib 512 \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
.fi
.PP
Inspect and resume a saved run without overriding its controls:
.PP
.nf
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-list \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-status RUN_UUID \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-resume RUN_UUID \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR liuxin (1),
.BR liuxin-ingest (1),
.BR wget (1)
.PP
